{
  "dom_id": "step-q108543",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "In a factory, two machines independently produce the same product. The random variable $X$ represents the number of rejects per day of the first machine, and the random\nvariable $Y$ is the number of rejects per day on another machine. The probability distributions of $X$ and $Y$ are given below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n\n<th>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$f(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>\n\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nCalculate the expected number of items per day that the factory rejects.",
  "worked_solution": "We need to calculate $\\text{E}[X+Y].$\n\nRecall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables (not necessarily independent), and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[aX+bY]=a\\text{E}[X]+b\\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nThe expected values of $X$ and $Y$ are calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot 0.1+1\\cdot 0.6+2\\cdot 0.2+3\\cdot 0.1=1.3 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & =0\\cdot 0.5+1\\cdot 0.3+2\\cdot 0.2=0.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X+Y]=\\text{E}[X]+\\text{E}[Y]=1.3+0.7=2.\n$$",
